### `333 status`: what this node's own record says about this node.
##
## A line here ends in `{` and the next begins with `""}` where the printed line
## is wider than a line of this file may be: a placeable may span two lines of
## the file, and what it prints has no line break in it.

status-yourself-on-no-roll = You are on nobody's roll. Nobody has handed you the file, so there is
    nothing yet for anyone to witness. `333 join` is the whole of it, and {
    ""}it
    needs an invitation from somebody who already has it.
    { $place } says what this is and where the code is. It cannot hand you the file.

status-yourself-not-yet-counted = Given the file in epoch { $joined }, and counted from epoch { $counted_from } — { $to_go } to go.
    Answer everything asked of you until then. None of it is banked, and {
    ""}all
    of it is watched.

status-yourself-says-nothing = Your record says nothing at all about { $missing } of those { $window } epochs.
    Nothing here turns that into an absence — a record can only say what {
    ""}a node
    was there to write. It is also why this ratio is not what anybody {
    ""}else reads
    you by: what they read is what they were told about you, by whoever was
    drawn to ask.

status-yourself-only-your-word = Nobody has yet signed anything about you, so for now there is only {
    ""}your own
    word for any of it.

status-yourself-checkable = The part of it anybody else can check is what others signed about you.
    { $witnessed } of those are here, kept after the epochs they belong to are gone.

status-yourself-record = Your record is what you wrote down about yourself, in order, signed {
    ""}as you
    went. Every answer you have ever given named where it stood at that {
    ""}moment, so
    its length and its order are not yours to change now. What it {
    ""}concludes is
    still your own word. { $checkable }

    Those signatures stay valid for ever. What cannot be recovered is {
    ""}whether the
    people who made them were of us at the time — by then they are gone, {
    ""}and there
    is nobody left to ask. A hundred-year-old record proves that somebody {
    ""}holding
    that key stood behind you, and stops there. 333 does not fix this and {
    ""}does not
    pretend to. The fix is a register of who was true, kept by somebody, {
    ""}for ever,
    and that is the one thing this network will not build.

status-yourself-never-asked = Nothing in the last { $window } epochs was ever put to you. Nobody was
    drawn to ask, so there is nothing to have failed. You are neither {
    ""}kept nor
    lapsed; you are simply not yet part of anybody's arithmetic.

status-yourself-counted = By your own record, you are counted.

status-yourself-not-counted = By your own record, you are not counted. Two of every three is the {
    ""}whole of
    what is asked.
    Nothing here is being served out. The window moves every epoch, and {
    ""}each one
    you answer pushes an older absence past its edge. Your chain still {
    ""}holds every
    hour you missed. The count does not reach back for them.

status-yourself-standing = Present in { $present } of the { $counted } epochs your record covers — { $share }. { $verdict }
    The window is the last { $window } epochs and nothing before it exists.
    Ten years of it would read exactly the same, and buy exactly as much; {
    ""}a year
    away and an hour away read exactly the same too, and cost exactly as {
    ""}little.

status-yourself-given-by-nobody = You hold the file, and nobody handed it to you, so you are on nobody's
    roll. Nobody goes out to ask a node on no roll, and nobody counts what
    it says, which is why `333 say` is refused. What you can do is hand the
    file on: whoever you hand it to is admitted, with both of you signing,
    and is counted from then.
